       <descriptionSet>
             <display>Falaj(pl. aflaj) irrigation channel that sinuously winds along a terraced garden with date palm
                 plantation along the rock incline. The falaj channel in Wādī Ghul, the highest canyon in Oman, is cut into the mountainside rock.
                 Its construction acts as an earth-retaining structure, forming one of the several terraces that make up
                 the oasis in this and many other mountain settlements in the upper reaches of Al Jabal al Akhḑar
                 mountains.</display>
             <description source="Bandyopadhyay, Soumyen, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3231-9166">Falaj(pl. aflaj) irrigation channel that sinuously winds along a terraced garden with date palm
                 plantation along the rock incline. The falaj channel in Wādī Ghul, the highest canyon in Oman, is cut into the mountainside rock.
                 Its construction acts as an earth-retaining structure, forming one of the several terraces that make up
                 the oasis in this and many other mountain settlements in the upper reaches of Al Jabal al Akhḑar
                 mountains.
             </description>
       </descriptionSet>
